IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`

-- ccc24-ministerial-review.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part XXI.1 (Applications for Ministerial Review -- Miscarriages of Justice,
-- sections 696.1 to 696.6) and Part XXI.2 (Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission, sections 696.7 to 696.87).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), part agent ccc24. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How to read an answer: see the header of ccc24-appeal-procedure.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING; a caller must never turn NOTHING into JUST FALSE).
-- Machinery left inert (reason 2 of the brief) and recorded in the coverage table, not here: section 696.6 (regulation-making power), section 696.71 (the Commission's
-- establishment, composition and head office), sections 696.73 to 696.79 (commissioners: diversity, qualifications, terms, removal, pay, meetings, quorum) and section 696.86 (staff).

§ `Part XXI.1 -- Applications for Ministerial Review -- Miscarriages of Justice (sections 696.1 to 696.6)`

§§ `Section 696.1 -- Application`

-- 696.1(1): "may be made ... by or on behalf of a person who has been convicted ... or has been found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender ... and whose rights ... have been exhausted".
-- The relative clauses name who may apply, with no "only": a person outside them is NOT COVERED (limited by its own wording).
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14391 | 696.1 (1) An application for ministerial review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Minister of Justice by or on behalf of a person who has been convicted of an offence under an Act of Parliament or a regulation made under an Act of Parliament or has been found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender under Part XXIV and whose rights of judicial review or appeal with respect to the conviction or finding have been exhausted.
@ref s 696.1(1) (src:14391-14391)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of an offence under an Act of Parliament or a regulation made under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender under Part XXIV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights of judicial review or appeal with respect to the conviction or finding have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.1(1) an application for ministerial review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Minister of Justice` MEANS
    IF (`the person has been convicted of an offence under an Act of Parliament or a regulation made under an Act of Parliament` OR `the person has been found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender under Part XXIV`)
       AND `the rights of judicial review or appeal with respect to the conviction or finding have been exhausted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whose rights of judicial review or appeal with respect to the conviction or finding have been exhausted"

-- src:14393 | (2) The application must be in the form, contain the information and be accompanied by any documents prescribed by the regulations.
@ref s 696.1(2) (src:14393-14393)
GIVEN `the application is in the form prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains the information prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by the documents prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.1(2) the application is in the form, contains the information and is accompanied by the documents prescribed by the regulations` MEANS
    IF `the application is in the form prescribed by the regulations` AND `the application contains the information prescribed by the regulations` AND `the application is accompanied by the documents prescribed by the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The application must be in the form, contain the information and be accompanied by any documents prescribed by the regulations"

§§ `Section 696.2 -- Review of applications`

-- src:14395 | 696.2 (1) On receipt of an application under this Part, the Minister of Justice shall review it in accordance with the regulations.
@ref s 696.2(1) (src:14395-14395)
GIVEN `the Minister of Justice has received an application under Part XXI.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.2(1) the Minister of Justice must review the application in accordance with the regulations` MEANS
    IF `the Minister of Justice has received an application under Part XXI.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On receipt of an application under this Part"

-- src:14397 | (2) For the purpose of any investigation in relation to an application under this Part, the Minister of Justice has and may exercise the powers of a commissioner under Part I of the Inquiries Act and the powers that may be conferred on a commissioner under section 11 of that Act.
@ref s 696.2(2) (src:14397-14397)
GIVEN `the purpose is an investigation in relation to an application under Part XXI.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.2(2) the Minister of Justice has and may exercise the powers of a commissioner under Part I of the Inquiries Act and the powers that may be conferred on a commissioner under section 11 of that Act` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is an investigation in relation to an application under Part XXI.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of any investigation in relation to an application under this Part"

-- 696.2(3): the delegate must be one of three kinds; the third kind is defined by the Minister's own opinion, which is a plain input.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14399 | (3) Despite subsection 11(3) of the Inquiries Act, the Minister of Justice may delegate in writing to any member in good standing of the bar of a province, retired judge or any other individual who, in the opinion of the Minister, has similar background or experience the powers of the Minister to take evidence, issue subpoenas, enforce the attendance of witnesses, compel them to give evidence and otherwise conduct an investigation under subsection (2).
@ref s 696.2(3) (src:14399-14399)
GIVEN `the delegation is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegate is a member in good standing of the bar of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegate is a retired judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Minister the delegate is another individual who has similar background or experience` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.2(3) the Minister of Justice may delegate the Minister's powers to take evidence, issue subpoenas, enforce the attendance of witnesses, compel them to give evidence and otherwise conduct an investigation under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF    `the delegation is in writing`
      AND (   `the delegate is a member in good standing of the bar of a province`
           OR `the delegate is a retired judge`
           OR `in the opinion of the Minister the delegate is another individual who has similar background or experience`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may delegate in writing to any member in good standing of the bar of a province, retired judge or any other individual who, in the opinion of the Minister, has similar background or experience"

§§ `Section 696.3 -- Reference to the court of appeal; the Minister's decision`

-- 696.3(1): "means" a definition, built on section 2's court of appeal (the keel's `s 2 court of appeal`, called here).
-- @tag fork=F673a
-- src:14401 | 696.3 (1) In this section, the court of appeal means the court of appeal, as defined by the definition court of appeal in section 2, for the province in which the person to whom an application under this Part relates was tried.
@ref s 696.3(1) (src:14401-14401)
GIVEN `it is the Court of Appeal of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is the one for the province in which the person to whom the application relates was tried` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.3(1) court of appeal` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is the one for the province in which the person to whom the application relates was tried`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court of appeal means the court of appeal, as defined by the definition court of appeal in section 2, for the province"
    ELSE `s 2 court of appeal` `it is the Court of Appeal of the province`

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14403 | (2) The Minister of Justice may, at any time, refer to the court of appeal, for its opinion, any question in relation to an application under this Part on which the Minister desires the assistance of that court, and the court shall furnish its opinion accordingly.
@ref s 696.3(2) (src:14403-14403)
GIVEN `the question is in relation to an application under Part XXI.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister desires the assistance of the court of appeal on the question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.3(2) the Minister of Justice may refer a question to the court of appeal for its opinion` MEANS
    IF `the question is in relation to an application under Part XXI.1` AND `the Minister desires the assistance of the court of appeal on the question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any question in relation to an application under this Part on which the Minister desires the assistance of that court"

-- src:14403 | (2) The Minister of Justice may, at any time, refer to the court of appeal, for its opinion, any question in relation to an application under this Part on which the Minister desires the assistance of that court, and the court shall furnish its opinion accordingly.
@ref s 696.3(2) (src:14403-14403)
GIVEN `the Minister of Justice has referred a question to the court of appeal under subsection 696.3(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.3(2) the court of appeal must furnish its opinion` MEANS
    IF `the Minister of Justice has referred a question to the court of appeal under subsection 696.3(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and the court shall furnish its opinion accordingly"

DECLARE `s 696.3(3) step` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.3(3)(a)(i) direct a new trial before any court that the Minister thinks proper`
    `s 696.3(3)(a)(i) direct a new hearing under Part XXIV`
    `s 696.3(3)(a)(ii) refer the matter to the court of appeal for hearing and determination as if it were an appeal`
    `s 696.3(3)(b) dismiss the application`
    `s 696.3(3) another step`

-- The two (a) steps need "satisfied that there is a reasonable basis to conclude that a miscarriage of justice likely occurred"; (b) needs only an application.
-- A new hearing is for "a person found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender under Part XXIV".
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14405 | (3) On an application under this Part, the Minister of Justice may
-- src:14406 | (a) if the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable basis to conclude that a miscarriage of justice likely occurred,
-- src:14407 | (i) direct, by order in writing, a new trial before any court that the Minister thinks proper or, in the case of a person found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender under Part XXIV, a new hearing under that Part, or
-- src:14408 | (ii) refer the matter at any time to the court of appeal for hearing and determination by that court as if it were an appeal by the convicted person or the person found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender under Part XXIV, as the case may be; or
-- src:14409 | (b) dismiss the application.
@ref s 696.3(3) (src:14405-14409)
GIVEN step IS A `s 696.3(3) step`
      `the Minister has an application under Part XXI.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable basis to conclude that a miscarriage of justice likely occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender under Part XXIV` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.3(3) the Minister of Justice may take the step on the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Minister has an application under Part XXI.1`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an application under this Part"
        IF step EQUALS `s 696.3(3) another step`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the Minister of Justice may"
        IF step EQUALS `s 696.3(3)(b) dismiss the application`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable basis to conclude that a miscarriage of justice likely occurred`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable basis to conclude that a miscarriage of justice likely occurred"
        IF step EQUALS `s 696.3(3)(a)(i) direct a new hearing under Part XXIV` AND (NOT `the person has been found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender under Part XXIV`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a person found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender under Part XXIV, a new hearing under that Part"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 696.3(4): "is final and is not subject to appeal" for a decision made under subsection (3); a decision of another kind is not mentioned.
-- src:14411 | (4) A decision of the Minister of Justice made under subsection (3) is final and is not subject to appeal.
@ref s 696.3(4) (src:14411-14411)
GIVEN `the decision was made by the Minister of Justice under subsection 696.3(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.3(4) the decision of the Minister of Justice is final and is not subject to appeal` MEANS
    IF `the decision was made by the Minister of Justice under subsection 696.3(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A decision of the Minister of Justice made under subsection (3) is final and is not subject to appeal"

§§ `Section 696.4 -- Considerations`

DECLARE `s 696.4 matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.4(a) whether the application is supported by new matters of significance that were not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Minister`
    `s 696.4(b) the relevance and reliability of information that is presented in connection with the application`
    `s 696.4(c) the fact that an application is not intended to serve as a further appeal and any remedy available on it is an extraordinary remedy`
    `s 696.4 another matter`

-- "all matters that the Minister considers relevant, including (a), (b) and (c)": the three are named, any other relevant matter is also to be taken into account.
-- src:14413 | 696.4 In making a decision under subsection 696.3(3), the Minister of Justice shall take into account all matters that the Minister considers relevant, including
-- src:14414 | (a) whether the application is supported by new matters of significance that were not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Minister in an application in relation to the same conviction or finding under Part XXIV;
-- src:14415 | (b) the relevance and reliability of information that is presented in connection with the application; and
-- src:14416 | (c) the fact that an application under this Part is not intended to serve as a further appeal and any remedy available on such an application is an extraordinary remedy.
@ref s 696.4 (src:14413-14416)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 696.4 matter`
      `the decision is a decision under subsection 696.3(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister considers the matter relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.4 the Minister of Justice must take the matter into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is a decision under subsection 696.3(3)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In making a decision under subsection 696.3(3)"
        IF matter EQUALS `s 696.4 another matter`
        THEN (IF `the Minister considers the matter relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all matters that the Minister considers relevant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 696.5 -- Annual report`

-- The period is fixed ("within six months after the end of each financial year"): a report later than that answers JUST FALSE (ruling (a) on periods).
-- Before six months have run and with no report yet, the text is silent: NOTHING.
-- @tag fork=F696m
-- src:14418 | 696.5 The Minister of Justice shall within six months after the end of each financial year submit an annual report to Parliament in relation to applications under this Part.
@ref s 696.5 (src:14418-14418)
GIVEN `the report has been submitted to Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months after the end of the financial year at which the report was submitted, or at which it is being asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.5 the Minister of Justice submitted the annual report in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report has been submitted to Parliament` AND `the number of months after the end of the financial year at which the report was submitted, or at which it is being asked about` AT MOST 6
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the number of months after the end of the financial year at which the report was submitted, or at which it is being asked about` GREATER THAN 6
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within six months after the end of each financial year"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within six months after the end of each financial year"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule.  The unit of time is the month (assumed, not ruled: the text gives six months).
DECLARE `s 696.5 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.5 submit the annual report to Parliament`

-- @tag fork=F696m
@ref s 696.5 (src:14418-14418)
`s 696.5 the annual report rule` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister of Justice`
    MUST `s 696.5 submit the annual report to Parliament`
    WITHIN 6
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister of Justice` BECAUSE "the annual report was not submitted to Parliament within six months after the end of the financial year"

§ `Part XXI.2 -- Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission (sections 696.7 to 696.87)`

§§ `Section 696.7 -- Definitions`

-- src:14430 | applicant in relation to a miscarriage of justice review application made to the Commission, means the person who is the subject of the finding or verdict in question. (demandeur)
@ref s 696.7 "applicant" (src:14430-14430)
GIVEN `the person is the subject of the finding or verdict in question in a miscarriage of justice review application made to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.7 applicant` MEANS
    IF `the person is the subject of the finding or verdict in question in a miscarriage of justice review application made to the Commission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applicant in relation to a miscarriage of justice review application made to the Commission, means the person who is the subject of the finding or verdict in question"

-- src:14431 | Commission means the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1). (Commission)
@ref s 696.7 "Commission" (src:14431-14431)
GIVEN `the body is the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.7 Commission` MEANS
    IF `the body is the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Commission means the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1)"

-- src:14432 | Minister means the Minister of Justice. (ministre)
@ref s 696.7 "Minister" (src:14432-14432)
GIVEN `the person is the Minister of Justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.7 Minister` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Minister of Justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Minister means the Minister of Justice"

§§ `Section 696.72 -- Mandate`

-- "after section 3 of the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission Act (David and Joyce Milgaard's Law) comes into force": whether it is in force is a plain input.
-- src:14442 | 696.72 The Commission’s mandate is to
-- src:14443 | (a) review applications made under Part XXI.1 on the grounds of miscarriage of justice after section 3 of the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission Act (David and Joyce Milgaard’s Law) comes into force;
@ref s 696.72(a) (src:14442-14443)
GIVEN `the application was made under Part XXI.1 on the grounds of miscarriage of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 3 of the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission Act (David and Joyce Milgaard's Law) has come into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.72(a) the Commission's mandate is to review the application` MEANS
    IF `the application was made under Part XXI.1 on the grounds of miscarriage of justice` AND `section 3 of the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission Act (David and Joyce Milgaard's Law) has come into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Commission's mandate is to"

-- src:14442 | 696.72 The Commission’s mandate is to
-- src:14443 | (a) review applications made under Part XXI.1 on the grounds of miscarriage of justice after section 3 of the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission Act (David and Joyce Milgaard’s Law) comes into force;
-- src:14444 | (b) make recommendations to address systemic issues that may lead to miscarriages of justice to relevant public authorities and bodies, including the Law Commission of Canada, federal-provincial-territorial committees and working groups, federal departments and agencies and parliamentary committees.
@ref s 696.72(b) (src:14442-14444)
GIVEN `the recommendation addresses systemic issues that may lead to miscarriages of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recommendation is made to a relevant public authority or body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.72(b) the Commission's mandate is to make a recommendation to a relevant public authority or body` MEANS
    IF `the recommendation addresses systemic issues that may lead to miscarriages of justice` AND `the recommendation is made to a relevant public authority or body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "make recommendations to address systemic issues that may lead to miscarriages of justice to relevant public authorities and bodies"

§§ `Section 696.8 to 696.85 -- Powers, duties and functions`

-- Duties owed to the public are answered as compliance: JUST TRUE where the stated manner is met, NOTHING where it is not (the text says "must", it does not say no).
-- src:14482 | 696.8 The Commission must ensure that applicants and potential applicants are able to communicate readily with the Commission from any place in Canada.
@ref s 696.8 (src:14482-14482)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant or a potential applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is able to communicate readily with the Commission from the place in Canada where the person is` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.8 the Commission has ensured that the person is able to communicate readily with the Commission from any place in Canada` MEANS
    IF `the person is an applicant or a potential applicant` AND `the person is able to communicate readily with the Commission from the place in Canada where the person is`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applicants and potential applicants are able to communicate readily with the Commission from any place in Canada"

-- src:14484 | 696.81 The Commission must publish information about its mandate on its website and must provide the public, including potential applicants, with information about its mandate and about miscarriages of justice.
@ref s 696.81 (src:14484-14484)
GIVEN `the Commission has published information about its mandate on its website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has provided the public, including potential applicants, with information about its mandate and about miscarriages of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.81 the Commission has published information about its mandate on its website and has provided the public with information about its mandate and about miscarriages of justice` MEANS
    IF `the Commission has published information about its mandate on its website` AND `the Commission has provided the public, including potential applicants, with information about its mandate and about miscarriages of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must publish information about its mandate on its website and must provide the public, including potential applicants, with information about its mandate and about miscarriages of justice"

-- src:14486 | 696.82 (1) The Commission must carry out its mandate in a transparent manner.
@ref s 696.82(1) (src:14486-14486)
GIVEN `the Commission carries out its mandate in a transparent manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.82(1) the Commission carries out its mandate in a transparent manner` MEANS
    IF `the Commission carries out its mandate in a transparent manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Commission must carry out its mandate in a transparent manner"

-- src:14488 | (2) The Commission must publish its decisions on its website in a manner that
-- src:14489 | (a) protects confidential information; and
-- src:14490 | (b) is not likely to interfere with the proper administration of justice in relation to a matter that the Commission directs to a court for a new trial or hearing or a matter that the Commission refers to a court of appeal for a hearing and determination.
@ref s 696.82(2) (src:14488-14490)
GIVEN `the Commission has published its decisions on its website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner of publication protects confidential information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner of publication is not likely to interfere with the proper administration of justice in relation to a matter that the Commission directs to a court for a new trial or hearing or refers to a court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.82(2) the Commission has published its decisions on its website in the manner the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the Commission has published its decisions on its website` AND `the manner of publication protects confidential information` AND `the manner of publication is not likely to interfere with the proper administration of justice in relation to a matter that the Commission directs to a court for a new trial or hearing or refers to a court of appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Commission must publish its decisions on its website in a manner that"

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14492 | 696.83 (1) The Commission may adopt policies generally for the carrying out of its work and the management of its affairs, including policies respecting its procedures and practices.
@ref s 696.83(1) (src:14492-14492)
GIVEN `the policy is for the carrying out of its work or the management of its affairs, including its procedures and practices` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.83(1) the Commission may adopt the policy` MEANS
    IF `the policy is for the carrying out of its work or the management of its affairs, including its procedures and practices`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may adopt policies generally for the carrying out of its work and the management of its affairs, including policies respecting its procedures and practices"

DECLARE `s 696.83(2) subject` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.83(2)(a) the making of applications`
    `s 696.83(2)(b) each stage of the review process`
    `s 696.83(2)(c) applications that are made on behalf of persons`
    `s 696.83(2)(d) the provision of notices and other information to applicants, to their representatives, to attorneys general and to other interested persons, including victims`
    `s 696.83(2)(e) meetings of the Commission`
    `s 696.83(2) another subject`

-- src:14494 | (2) The Commission must adopt policies respecting
-- src:14495 | (a) the making of applications;
-- src:14496 | (b) each stage of the review process;
-- src:14497 | (c) applications that are made on behalf of persons;
-- src:14498 | (d) the provision of notices and other information to applicants, to their representatives, to attorneys general and to other interested persons, including victims; and
-- src:14499 | (e) meetings of the Commission.
@ref s 696.83(2) (src:14494-14499)
GIVEN subject IS A `s 696.83(2) subject`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.83(2) the Commission must adopt policies respecting the subject` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
    WHEN `s 696.83(2) another subject` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The Commission must adopt policies respecting"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:14501 | (3) The Commission must publish its policies on its website.
@ref s 696.83(3) (src:14501-14501)
GIVEN `the Commission has published its policies on its website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.83(3) the Commission has published its policies on its website` MEANS
    IF `the Commission has published its policies on its website`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Commission must publish its policies on its website"

-- 696.83(4): "does not apply" is a flat negative: JUST FALSE for a policy the Commission adopted.
-- src:14503 | (4) The Statutory Instruments Act does not apply to policies adopted by the Commission.
@ref s 696.83(4) (src:14503-14503)
GIVEN `the policy is a policy adopted by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.83(4) the Statutory Instruments Act applies to the policy` MEANS
    IF `the policy is a policy adopted by the Commission`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Statutory Instruments Act does not apply to policies adopted by the Commission"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "The Statutory Instruments Act does not apply to policies adopted by the Commission"

DECLARE `s 696.84(1) power` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.84(1)(a) direct employees to provide applicants and potential applicants with general information and guidance on applications and each stage of the review process`
    `s 696.84(1)(a.1) direct employees to notify the Correctional Service of Canada and the Parole Board of Canada of the importance of ensuring that applicants and potential applicants do not experience barriers`
    `s 696.84(1)(b) enter into contracts in its own name`
    `s 696.84(1)(c) provide supports to applicants in need`
    `s 696.84(1)(d) enter into contracts with persons who have technical or specialized knowledge to assist in the Commission's work`
    `s 696.84(1) another power`

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14505 | 696.84 (1) The Commission may, in carrying out its mandate,
-- src:14506 | (a) direct employees to provide applicants and potential applicants with general information and guidance on applications and each stage of the review process;
-- src:14507 | (a.1) direct employees to notify the Correctional Service of Canada and the Parole Board of Canada of the importance of ensuring that applicants and potential applicants do not experience barriers to or exclusion from programs, services or conditional release processes as a result of making an application for a review on the grounds of a miscarriage of justice;
-- src:14508 | (b) enter into contracts in its own name;
-- src:14509 | (c) provide supports to applicants in need, including by entering into contracts with service providers for the provision of those supports; and
-- src:14510 | (d) enter into contracts with persons who have technical or specialized knowledge to assist in the Commission’s work.
@ref s 696.84(1) (src:14505-14510)
GIVEN power IS A `s 696.84(1) power`
      `the Commission is carrying out its mandate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supports are for an applicant in need` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is with a person who has technical or specialized knowledge to assist in the Commission's work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.84(1) the Commission may exercise the power in carrying out its mandate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Commission is carrying out its mandate`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in carrying out its mandate"
        IF power EQUALS `s 696.84(1) another power`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The Commission may, in carrying out its mandate"
        IF power EQUALS `s 696.84(1)(c) provide supports to applicants in need` AND (NOT `the supports are for an applicant in need`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "provide supports to applicants in need"
        IF power EQUALS `s 696.84(1)(d) enter into contracts with persons who have technical or specialized knowledge to assist in the Commission's work` AND (NOT `the contract is with a person who has technical or specialized knowledge to assist in the Commission's work`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "enter into contracts with persons who have technical or specialized knowledge to assist in the Commission’s work"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 696.84(2) support` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.84(2)(a) directing them to services in their communities for persons in need or helping them access those services`
    `s 696.84(2)(b) providing them with translation and interpretation services`
    `s 696.84(2)(c) assisting them in relation to necessities such as food and housing`
    `s 696.84(2)(d) assisting them in obtaining legal assistance in relation to making an application or providing a written response to an investigation report prepared by the Commission`
    `s 696.84(2) another support`

-- "include": the list is not closed.  (c) and (d) are given "if they are without means".
-- src:14512 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), supports to applicants in need include
-- src:14513 | (a) directing them to services in their communities for persons in need or helping them access those services;
-- src:14514 | (b) providing them with translation and interpretation services;
-- src:14515 | (c) assisting them, if they are without means, in relation to necessities such as food and housing; and
-- src:14516 | (d) assisting them, if they are without means, in obtaining legal assistance in relation to making an application or providing a written response to an investigation report prepared by the Commission.
@ref s 696.84(2) (src:14512-14516)
GIVEN support IS A `s 696.84(2) support`
      `the person is an applicant in need` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is without means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is an applicant in need`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "supports to applicants in need include"
        IF support EQUALS `s 696.84(2) another support`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "include"
        IF (support EQUALS `s 696.84(2)(c) assisting them in relation to necessities such as food and housing` OR support EQUALS `s 696.84(2)(d) assisting them in obtaining legal assistance in relation to making an application or providing a written response to an investigation report prepared by the Commission`)
           AND (NOT `the applicant is without means`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if they are without means"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:14518 | 696.85 The Commission and its employees must follow established procedures and practices, including any requirement found in a Treasury Board policy or directive, for the secure handling, storage, transportation and transmission of information or documents.
@ref s 696.85 (src:14518-14518)
GIVEN `the Commission and its employees have followed established procedures and practices for the secure handling, storage, transportation and transmission of information or documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.85 the Commission and its employees have followed established procedures and practices for the secure handling, storage, transportation and transmission of information or documents` MEANS
    IF `the Commission and its employees have followed established procedures and practices for the secure handling, storage, transportation and transmission of information or documents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must follow established procedures and practices, including any requirement found in a Treasury Board policy or directive, for the secure handling, storage, transportation and transmission of information or documents"

§§ `Section 696.87 -- Annual report of the Commission`

-- 696.87(1): "within five months after the end of each fiscal year": a fixed period, as for section 696.5.
-- src:14526 | 696.87 (1) The Chief Commissioner must, within five months after the end of each fiscal year, submit to the Minister a report that contains the following information for that fiscal year:
@ref s 696.87(1) period (src:14526-14526)
GIVEN `the report has been submitted to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months after the end of the fiscal year at which the report was submitted, or at which it is being asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.87(1) the Chief Commissioner submitted the report in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report has been submitted to the Minister` AND `the number of months after the end of the fiscal year at which the report was submitted, or at which it is being asked about` AT MOST 5
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the number of months after the end of the fiscal year at which the report was submitted, or at which it is being asked about` GREATER THAN 5
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within five months after the end of each fiscal year"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within five months after the end of each fiscal year"

DECLARE `s 696.87(1) item` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.87(1)(a) the number of applications received`
    `s 696.87(1)(b) statistics on applicants that, to the extent possible, are disaggregated by gender identity, age, race, ethnic origin, language, disability, income and any other identity factor`
    `s 696.87(1)(c) the number of investigations started and the number of investigations completed`
    `s 696.87(1)(d) the number of matters that the Commission directed to courts for new trials or hearings`
    `s 696.87(1)(e) the number of matters that the Commission referred to courts of appeal for hearings and determinations`
    `s 696.87(1)(f) the number of applications dismissed`
    `s 696.87(1)(g) the outcomes of matters that the Commission directed to courts for new trials or hearings`
    `s 696.87(1)(h) the outcomes of matters that the Commission referred to courts of appeal for hearings and determinations`
    `s 696.87(1)(i) the average length of time between the receipt of an application and the Commission's final decision`
    `s 696.87(1)(j) the number of applicants in need who received supports`
    `s 696.87(1)(k) the amounts paid to service providers under paragraph 696.84(1)(c)`
    `s 696.87(1)(l) any other information on the Commission's activities that the Chief Commissioner considers relevant`
    `s 696.87(1) another item`

-- src:14527 | (a) the number of applications received;
-- src:14528 | (b) statistics on applicants that, to the extent possible, are disaggregated by gender identity, age, race, ethnic origin, language, disability, income and any other identity factor that is considered in the course of a gender-based analysis;
-- src:14529 | (c) the number of investigations started and the number of investigations completed;
-- src:14530 | (d) the number of matters that the Commission directed to courts for new trials or hearings;
-- src:14531 | (e) the number of matters that the Commission referred to courts of appeal for hearings and determinations;
-- src:14532 | (f) the number of applications dismissed;
-- src:14533 | (g) the outcomes of matters that the Commission directed to courts for new trials or hearings;
-- src:14534 | (h) the outcomes of matters that the Commission referred to courts of appeal for hearings and determinations;
-- src:14535 | (i) the average length of time between the receipt of an application and the Commission’s final decision;
-- src:14536 | (j) the number of applicants in need who received supports;
-- src:14537 | (k) the amounts paid to service providers under paragraph 696.84(1)(c), disaggregated, to the extent possible, by the nature of the supports provided by the service providers; and
-- src:14538 | (l) any other information on the Commission’s activities that the Chief Commissioner considers relevant.
@ref s 696.87(1) contents (src:14527-14538)
GIVEN item IS A `s 696.87(1) item`
      `the Chief Commissioner considers the information on the Commission's activities relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.87(1) the report must contain the item for that fiscal year` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 696.87(1) another item` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "contains the following information for that fiscal year"
    WHEN `s 696.87(1)(l) any other information on the Commission's activities that the Chief Commissioner considers relevant` THEN
        IF `the Chief Commissioner considers the information on the Commission's activities relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other information on the Commission’s activities that the Chief Commissioner considers relevant"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 696.87(2): "on any of the first 30 days on which that House is sitting after the day on which the report is received": a fixed window in sitting days.
-- src:14540 | (2) The Minister must cause the report to be laid before each House of Parliament on any of the first 30 days on which that House is sitting after the day on which the report is received.
@ref s 696.87(2) (src:14540-14540)
GIVEN `the report has been laid before the House` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of sitting days of the House after the day on which the report was received, counted to the day on which it was laid or is being asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.87(2) the Minister caused the report to be laid before the House in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report has been laid before the House` AND `the number of sitting days of the House after the day on which the report was received, counted to the day on which it was laid or is being asked about` AT MOST 30
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the number of sitting days of the House after the day on which the report was received, counted to the day on which it was laid or is being asked about` GREATER THAN 30
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on any of the first 30 days on which that House is sitting after the day on which the report is received"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on any of the first 30 days on which that House is sitting"

-- src:14542 | (3) The Commission must publish the annual report on its website after it has been tabled.
@ref s 696.87(3) (src:14542-14542)
GIVEN `the annual report has been tabled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.87(3) the Commission must publish the annual report on its website` MEANS
    IF `the annual report has been tabled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Commission must publish the annual report on its website after it has been tabled"
